# Web App / Cookie Bridge Architecture in 9Router

Use this rule whenever integrating or debugging web-only AI providers (e.g. Composio Bench, Grok Web, Perplexity Web).

## 1. Wire Capture Over Assumptions
- Never assume an upstream platform exposes standard `/v1/chat/completions`.
- Always inspect the live browser network payload (e.g. `POST /api/arena`, `/rest/app-chat`, `/rest/sse/perplexity_ask`).
- Extract the exact session cookie key (e.g. `wos-session=...`, `sso=...`, `__Secure-next-auth.session-token=...`).

## 2. Executor Stream Translation (`open-sse/executors/{id}-web.js`)
- Subclass `BaseExecutor`.
- Translate client OpenAI `messages` array into the platform's JSON format.
- Stream responses back into standard OpenAI SSE chunks (`chat.completion.chunk`) with `delta.content` and `delta.reasoning_content`.
- Implement non-streaming fallback (`stream: false`) by collecting chunks and returning an OpenAI `chat.completion` response.

## 3. Rate-Limit & Conversation ID Reuse
- If the upstream service limits new chats (e.g. Composio's 10-new-chats/day limit):
  - Capture and cache the response conversation ID (e.g. `x-conversation-id` header).
  - Forward the cached ID in subsequent requests to maintain an active thread and bypass the new-chat rate limit.

## 4. Connection Probe Classification (`src/lib/providers/connectionProbe.js`)
- Register a dedicated probe in `ADAPTERS["{id}"]`.
- Treat `HTTP 200` as valid.
- Treat `HTTP 429` as `valid: true` with a soft warning (the session is authenticated, but rate-limited).
- Only treat `HTTP 401` and `HTTP 403` as `valid: false` (session expired or missing).

## 5. UI Placement
- Register with `category: "apikey"` in `open-sse/providers/registry/{id}.js` so the provider renders immediately in the main Providers grid on `/dashboard/providers`.
